{"id":"b302bf24-ba8b-4bb4-83f4-84cefa30c625","object":"chat.completion","created":1784988466,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    segments = case['segments']\\n    budget = case['budget']\\n    if budget < sum(s['minimum'] for s in segments):\\n        raise ValueError('budget too low')\\n    if budget > sum(s['capacity'] for s in segments):\\n        raise ValueError('budget too high')\\n    alloc = [s['minimum'] for s in segments]\\n    rem = budget - sum(alloc)\\n    while rem > 0:\\n        best = None\\n        best_score = -1.0\\n        for i, s in enumerate(segments):\\n            if alloc[i] >= s['capacity']:\\n                continue\\n            score = s['importance'] / (alloc[i] + 1)\\n            if best is None or score > best_score + 1e-12:\\n                best = i\\n                best_score = score\\n            elif abs(score - best_score) < 1e-12 and i < best:\\n                best = i\\n                best_score = score\\n        if best is None:\\n            raise ValueError('cannot allocate more')\\n        alloc[best] += 1\\n        rem -= 1\\n    total = sum(alloc)\\n    by_name = {segments[i]['name']: alloc[i] for i in range(len(segments))}\\n    return {'allocations': alloc, 'by_name': by_name, 'total': total}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write a Python function `solve(case)` that follows the described behavior. The case has `segments` list, each with `name`, `importance`, `minimum`, `capacity`. Also `budget`. We must allocate tokens to segments: first give each its minimum, then distribute remaining budget one token at a time to segment with highest importance / (next allocated position). Break ties by original segment order (i.e., index in list). Return { \"allocations\": list of ints in same order as segments, \"by_name\": dict mapping name to allocation, \"total\": total allocated (should equal budget if feasible). 